        "section": "abstract-algebra",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Galois Theory",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "GALOIS EXTENSION: K/F is Galois if:\n  |Aut(K/F)| = [K:F].\n  Equivalently: K is the splitting field of a separable polynomial f ∈ F[x].\n  (Separable: no repeated roots — automatic in char 0 or over a perfect field; irreducible\n   polynomials over imperfect char-p fields can be inseparable, e.g. x^p − t over 𝔽_p(t).)"
    },
    {
      "id": "06-GALOIS-THEORY.md#009",
      "path": [
        "06-GALOIS-THEORY.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:abstract-algebra:06-galois-theory, git-history:abstract-algebra:06-galois-theory]",
        "canonical_path": "abstract-algebra/06-GALOIS-THEORY.md",
