        "section": "abstract-algebra",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Galois Theory",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "EXAMPLES:\n  Q(√2)/Q: Gal = {id, σ} where σ(√2) = -√2. ≅ Z/2Z.\n  Q(i)/Q: Gal = {id, σ} where σ(i) = -i (complex conjugation restricted). ≅ Z/2Z.\n  Q(ζₙ)/Q (cyclotomic): Gal ≅ (Z/nZ)*, order φ(n).\n    σₐ(ζₙ) = ζₙᵃ for each a ∈ (Z/nZ)*.\n  F_{p^n}/F_p: Gal = ⟨Frobenius⟩ ≅ Z/nZ.\n  Q(∛2, ω)/Q (ω = e^{2πi/3}): Gal = S_3. (Degree 6, symmetric group on roots.)\n```"
    },
